---
description: >
  Drops Codex spans that cannot reach an OCSF class. Codex instruments its
  HTTP/2 and async-runtime internals with spans such as `try_reclaim_frame`,
  `FramedRead::poll_next`, and `poll_ready`, which outnumber the
  security-relevant spans by roughly three orders of magnitude. Removing them
  before normalization avoids serializing every one into `raw_data` only to
  discard it after mapping. The conditions mirror what
  `openai::codex::ocsf::map` can actually map.
args:
  named:
    - name: name
      type: field
      default: event_name
      description: The field that holds the span name.
---

where $name.starts_with("codex.") or
      $name in [
        "built_tools",
        "endpoint_session.execute_with",
        "list_tools_for_server",
        "plugins_for_config",
        "recommended_plugins_mode_for_config",
        "session_task.turn",
      ] or
      attributes.tool_name? != null or
      attributes.file_operation? != null or
      attributes["rpc.method"]? != null or
      attributes["http.request.method"]? != null or
      attributes["http.method"]? != null or
      attributes["span.type"]? != null
